The design is an OrderedDict where the front is least recently used and the back is most recently used. A `get` that finds the key moves it to the back and returns its value, or returns -1 when the key is absent. A `put` on an existing key updates the value and moves it to the back. A `put` of a new key first evicts from the front while the cache is full, then inserts at the back. Because a capacity of 0 means nothing can ever be stored, `put` returns immediately in that case, so the eviction loop never runs against an empty dictionary.

